---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { articlePageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqPageSchema, webPageSchema } from "../../utils/schema";

const title = "Grey Rock Method: Low-Detail Replies for Bait and Drama";
const description = "Practical Grey Rock method examples, short replies, safety caveats, and scripts for low-detail mode when engagement gives pressure more material.";
const canonical = "/guides/grey-rock-method/";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Grey Rock rude?",
    "answer": "It can feel rude if the other person expects emotional access. But short is not automatically cruel. The question is whether the interaction deserves more access."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I use Grey Rock at work?",
    "answer": "Sometimes. It works best for bait, gossip, and unnecessary emotional arguments. For actual work decisions, use clear documentation and priority language instead."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I explain why I am using it?",
    "answer": "Usually no. Explaining Grey Rock defeats the point."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Grey Rock safe in abusive relationships?",
    "answer": "Not always. It can reduce conflict in some cases and escalate it in others. If safety is involved, get support beyond scripts."
  }
];
const jsonLd = [
  webPageSchema({ title, description, path: canonical }),
  articlePageSchema({ title, description, path: canonical, section: "Pillar Guide" }),
  breadcrumbSchema([{ name: "Guides", path: "/guides/" }, { name: title, path: canonical }]),
  ...(faqs.length ? [faqPageSchema(faqs, canonical)] : [])
];
const contentHtml = "<section class=\"manual-entry-section related-guide-links\"><p class=\"section-label\">Related Conflict Protocol pages</p><ul><li><a href=\"/patterns-and-techniques/grey-rock/\">Grey Rock</a></li><li><a href=\"/patterns-and-techniques/broken-record/\">Broken Record</a></li><li><a href=\"/patterns-and-techniques/no-jade/\">No Jade</a></li><li><a href=\"/patterns-and-techniques/boundary/\">Boundary</a></li><li><a href=\"/guides/stonewalling-silent-treatment-response/\">Stonewalling Silent Treatment Response</a></li></ul></section>\n<h2>Quick answer</h2>\n<p>Grey Rock is a response technique where you give low-emotion, low-detail replies so the other person has less to grab, twist, or escalate.</p>\n<p>It sounds like:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Okay.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Okay.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’ll handle it.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’ll handle it.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Noted.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Noted.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not discussing that.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not discussing that.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Grey Rock is not about being rude. It is about not feeding a conversation that feeds on reaction.</p>\n<p>Use it when more emotion, more explanation, or more personal detail makes the interaction worse.</p>\n<p>Do not use it when the situation needs warmth, repair, clarity, or safety planning.</p>\n<h2>What low-detail mode is</h2>\n<p>Some people use your reaction as fuel.</p>\n<p>If you explain, they pick apart the explanation. If you defend, they attack the defense. If you show hurt, they call you dramatic. If you get angry, they make your anger the story.</p>\n<p>Grey Rock lowers the available material.</p>\n<p>It says less. It gives fewer hooks. It does not perform closeness for someone using closeness against you.</p>\n<p>Grey Rock works best when the goal is not connection. The goal is to get through the interaction with minimal damage.</p>\n<h2>Grey Rock examples</h2>\n<h3>When they bait you</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“That’s your opinion.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“That’s your opinion.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Noted.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Noted.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not getting into that.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not getting into that.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>When they insult your tone</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Okay.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Okay.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’ll keep it brief.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’ll keep it brief.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“The answer is still NO.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“The answer is still NO.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>When they fish for details</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not sharing more detail.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not sharing more detail.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“That’s private.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“That’s private.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“The plan is already set.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“The plan is already set.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>When they start a character debate</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not discussing my character.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not discussing my character.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“That’s not the topic.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“That’s not the topic.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m going to stop here.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m going to stop here.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>When they repeat the ask</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“No.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“No.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not available.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not available.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’ve answered.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’ve answered.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h2>What Grey Rock is not</h2>\n<p>Grey Rock is not silent punishment.</p>\n<p>It is not disappearing to make someone anxious. It is not using coldness as revenge. It is not refusing to communicate with someone who is trying in good faith. It is not a replacement for a clear boundary.</p>\n<p>Grey Rock is a narrow tool for high-friction interactions where extra engagement makes things worse.</p>\n<p>If someone says, “I want to understand what happened,” Grey Rock may be the wrong tool.</p>\n<p>If someone says, “You’re insane and everyone agrees,” Grey Rock may be exactly enough.</p>\n<h2>When not to use Grey Rock</h2>\n<p>Do not use Grey Rock when:</p>\n<ul><li>you need to repair harm you caused</li><li>the other person is asking a fair question</li><li>a child needs warmth and explanation</li><li>the situation requires legal, HR, medical, or safety help</li><li>silence could escalate danger</li><li>you are using it to punish someone</li><li>the relationship actually needs an honest conversation</li></ul>\n<p>Grey Rock is also not always safe. In some controlling relationships, becoming less responsive can make the other person escalate.</p>\n<p>If you are afraid of the person, being monitored, threatened, or punished for setting limits, prioritize safety and outside support over technique.</p>\n<h2>Grey Rock vs boundary</h2>\n<p>A boundary says what you will or will not do.</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not discussing this tonight.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not discussing this tonight.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Grey Rock reduces the emotional surface area.</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Noted.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Noted.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Sometimes you use both:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not discussing this tonight.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not discussing this tonight.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Then, if they keep baiting:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Okay.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Okay.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Boundary sets the line. Grey Rock stops feeding the argument around the line.</p>\n<h2>Grey Rock vs stonewalling</h2>\n<p>Grey Rock is not the same as stonewalling.</p>\n<p>Stonewalling blocks a needed conversation and leaves the other person with no path forward.</p>\n<p>Grey Rock protects you in a conversation that has become bait, attack, or extraction.</p>\n<p>A useful test:</p>\n<p>Are you avoiding accountability, or are you avoiding a trap?</p>\n<p>If you harmed someone and refuse to talk, that is not Grey Rock. That is avoidance.</p>\n<p>If someone keeps using your words as weapons, Grey Rock may be protection.</p>\n<h2>What to text back</h2>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Short:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Noted.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Noted.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Neutral:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not discussing that by text.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not discussing that by text.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Firmer:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’ve answered. I’m not continuing this thread.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’ve answered. I’m not continuing this thread.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Logistics only:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Pickup is at 6. I’ll be there.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Pickup is at 6. I’ll be there.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Do not send:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m grey-rocking you because you’re toxic.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m grey-rocking you because you’re toxic.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>That gives them the reaction and the label. Grey Rock works because it does not announce itself.</p>\n<h2>Wrong vs better</h2>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Wrong:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I can’t believe you would say that. You always do this. I’m tired of being treated like I’m crazy.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I can’t believe you would say that. You always do this. I’m tired of being treated like I’m crazy.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Why it feeds the bait:</p>\n<p>The reply is understandable, but it gives them anger, history, and pain to use.</p>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Better:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not getting into that.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not getting into that.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p class=\"section-label\">Why it works:</p>\n<p>It gives them almost nothing to pull apart.</p>\n<h2>If they push back</h2>\n<p><strong>They say:</strong> “Why are you being so cold?” <strong>You say:</strong> “I’m keeping this brief.”</p>\n<p><strong>They say:</strong> “Say something.” <strong>You say:</strong> “I’ve answered.”</p>\n<p><strong>They say:</strong> “You think you’re better than me?” <strong>You say:</strong> “No.”</p>\n<p><strong>They say:</strong> “You’re impossible.” <strong>You say:</strong> “Okay.”</p>\n<p>This can feel unnatural. That is the point. You are not trying to satisfy the bait.</p>\n<h2>Grey Rock by context</h2>\n<h3>Family bait</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not discussing that today.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not discussing that today.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I hear you.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I hear you.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m going to help with dinner now.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m going to help with dinner now.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>Workplace bait</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Thanks for the feedback.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Thanks for the feedback.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Please send the request in writing.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Please send the request in writing.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’ll respond when the scope is clear.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’ll respond when the scope is clear.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>Friend drama</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not taking sides.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not taking sides.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“That sounds difficult.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“That sounds difficult.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not the right person for this conversation.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not the right person for this conversation.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h3>Co-parenting or logistics</h3>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Pickup is at 6.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Pickup is at 6.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Please use the shared calendar.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Please use the shared calendar.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’ll respond to schedule questions only.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’ll respond to schedule questions only.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h2>The Grey Rock tone</h2>\n<p>Grey Rock is plain.</p>\n<p>Not icy. Not sarcastic. Not theatrical.</p>\n<p>Think: boring receipt.</p>\n<p>A boring receipt does not defend itself. It does not explain why it is a receipt. It just shows the transaction.</p>\n<p>Your tone should be:</p>\n<ul><li>short</li><li>factual</li><li>low emotion</li><li>low detail</li><li>not contemptuous</li><li>not secretly trying to win</li></ul>\n<p>If you add contempt, it is no longer a grey rock. It is a thrown rock.</p>\n<h2>When Grey Rock becomes a problem</h2>\n<p>Grey Rock can become avoidance if you use it everywhere.</p>\n<p>If a safe person asks what hurt you, and you answer “noted,” you are not protecting yourself. You are shutting down.</p>\n<p>If a partner asks for repair after you snapped, Grey Rock is the wrong tool.</p>\n<p>If a coworker asks a real project question, Grey Rock makes you look evasive.</p>\n<p>Use the technique where it fits. Put it down where it does not.</p>\n<h2>When the script fails</h2>\n<p>If they escalate because you are less reactive:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not continuing this conversation.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not continuing this conversation.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>If they demand an emotional response:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m keeping this brief.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m keeping this brief.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>If they keep fishing for details:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not sharing more.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not sharing more.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>If the person becomes threatening, stop focusing on technique. Get distance, support, documentation, or emergency help as appropriate.</p>\n<h2>How to practice this</h2>\n<p>Practice making the reply shorter.</p>\n<p>Start with the messy version:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I don’t want to talk about this because every time we do, you twist it and I end up feeling horrible.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I don’t want to talk about this because every time we do, you twist it and I end up feeling horrible.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Shorter:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not discussing this.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not discussing this.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Even shorter:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“No.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“No.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Grey Rock is a deletion exercise.</p>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Announcing the technique.</li><li>Using sarcasm.</li><li>Giving one short line, then a long explanation.</li><li>Using Grey Rock when repair is needed.</li><li>Treating all conflict like bait.</li><li>Staying in unsafe situations because you are trying to be “low reaction.”</li></ul>\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n<h3>Is Grey Rock rude?</h3>\n<p>It can feel rude if the other person expects emotional access. But short is not automatically cruel. The question is whether the interaction deserves more access.</p>\n<h3>Can I use Grey Rock at work?</h3>\n<p>Sometimes. It works best for bait, gossip, and unnecessary emotional arguments. For actual work decisions, use clear documentation and priority language instead.</p>\n<h3>Should I explain why I am using it?</h3>\n<p>Usually no. Explaining Grey Rock defeats the point.</p>\n<h3>Is Grey Rock safe in abusive relationships?</h3>\n<p>Not always. It can reduce conflict in some cases and escalate it in others. If safety is involved, get support beyond scripts.</p>\n<h2>Extra copy-ready lines</h2>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not getting into that.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not getting into that.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’ll keep this brief.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’ll keep this brief.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“No, thank you.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“No, thank you.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“That does not work for me.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“That does not work for me.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m only discussing logistics.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m only discussing logistics.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Please send it in writing.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Please send it in writing.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<h2>The “good enough” reply</h2>\n<p>Grey Rock is hard for people who are used to proving good intent. You may feel rude, unfinished, or exposed.</p>\n<p>That is why the goal is not the best reply. The goal is a good enough reply that does not feed the bait.</p>\n<p>Good enough:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Okay.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Okay.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’ll think about it.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’ll think about it.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“No, thank you.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“No, thank you.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not discussing that.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not discussing that.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>The other person may dislike the lack of material. That does not mean you owe them more material.</p>\n<h2>Logistics mode</h2>\n<p>One of the safest Grey Rock versions is logistics mode. It is especially useful with coworkers, co-parents, roommates, and family members you cannot fully avoid.</p>\n<p>You only answer the practical part.</p>\n<p>They write:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“You’re always impossible. Anyway, what time are you coming?”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“You’re always impossible. Anyway, what time are you coming?”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>You answer:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’ll arrive at 6.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’ll arrive at 6.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>They write:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“Of course you ignore the main point.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“Of course you ignore the main point.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>You answer:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’ve answered the schedule question.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’ve answered the schedule question.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Logistics mode is not warm. It is not meant to be. It is meant to keep the interaction from becoming a feeding session.</p>\n<h2>A quick self-check</h2>\n<p>Before using Grey Rock, ask:</p>\n<ol><li>Is more explanation likely to help?</li><li>Is the person engaging in good faith?</li><li>Do I need to preserve a record?</li><li>Could low response escalate danger?</li><li>Am I doing this for protection, or punishment?</li></ol>\n<p>If the honest answer is punishment, choose another tool. If the honest answer is protection, keep it short.</p>\n<h2>Mini examples</h2>\n<p><strong>Bait:</strong> “You always think you’re better than everyone.” <strong>Grey Rock:</strong> “Okay.”</p>\n<p><strong>Bait:</strong> “Are you going to explain why you ignored me?” <strong>Grey Rock:</strong> “I’m not discussing that tonight.”</p>\n<p><strong>Bait:</strong> “Tell me where you’re going.” <strong>Grey Rock:</strong> “I have plans.”</p>\n<p><strong>Bait:</strong> “You’re so cold now.” <strong>Grey Rock:</strong> “I’m keeping this brief.”</p>\n<p><strong>Bait:</strong> “So you admit you were wrong?” <strong>Grey Rock:</strong> “No.”</p>\n<p>These lines may feel too small. That is usually why they work. They do not give the other person a full meal.</p>\n<h2>A note on warmth</h2>\n<p>Grey Rock is not the main tool for people who are safe, sincere, and confused. If someone you trust says, “I don’t understand what happened,” a warmer explanation may be appropriate.</p>\n<p>The mistake is using your best emotional openness with someone who repeatedly weaponizes it.</p>\n<p>Ask yourself:</p>\n<p>Has this person used my explanations fairly in the past?</p>\n<p>If yes, explain.</p>\n<p>If no, reduce the material.</p>\n<p>That is the heart of Grey Rock. Not coldness. Discernment.</p>\n<h2>If you accidentally react</h2>\n<p>You may not Grey Rock perfectly. You may take the bait, explain too much, snap, or send the paragraph. That does not ruin everything.</p>\n<p>Reset with one short line:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I’m not continuing this thread.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I’m not continuing this thread.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Or:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“I said more than I meant to. The short version is no.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“I said more than I meant to. The short version is no.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Do not punish yourself by staying in the argument because you already made one messy reply. The reset is allowed.</p>\n<p>A good practice is to write the long reply somewhere else first. Notes app. Draft. Paper. Anywhere that is not the thread. Then cut it to one line. Grey Rock is often easier after your nervous system has had somewhere to put the first wave.</p>\n<h2>The one-place rule</h2>\n<p>If you must give information, give it in one place and keep it factual.</p>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“The appointment is Thursday at 3.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“The appointment is Thursday at 3.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>Not:</p>\n<div class=\"copy-script-box\"><p>“The appointment is Thursday at 3, and I know you’ll probably complain, but this was the only time available, and I already tried to change it.”</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-line\" data-copy=\"“The appointment is Thursday at 3, and I know you’ll probably complain, but this was the only time available, and I already tried to change it.”\">Copy</button></div>\n<p>The second version gives them complaints, predictions, and your effort to judge. The first version gives them the appointment.</p>\n<p>Grey Rock is often less about silence and more about removing the extra emotional packaging.</p>\n<h2>Sources and further reading</h2>\n<p>Verified links for context and safety boundaries:</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.thehotline.org/resources/safety-planning-while-living-with-an-abusive-partner/\">The National Domestic Violence Hotline: Safety planning while living with an abusive partner</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.thehotline.org/identify-abuse/power-and-control/\">The National Domestic Violence Hotline: Power and control</a></li></ul>";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} image="/assets/articles/grey-rock-flat-reply.webp" bodyClass="editorial-page pillar-guide-page" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="answer-page pillar-guide">
    <header class="page-header shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Pillar guide</p>
      <h1>Grey Rock Method: Low-Detail Replies for Bait and Drama</h1>
      <div class="answer-lead">
        <p>{description}</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="shell-narrow article-body" set:html={contentHtml.replace(
      "<h2>Sources and further reading</h2>",
      `<h2>A realistic escalation</h2>
<ol><li><strong>Them:</strong> You’re being weird. Why are you so cold?</li><li><strong>You:</strong> I’m keeping this brief.</li><li><strong>Them:</strong> No, say what you really mean.</li><li><strong>You:</strong> I’ve answered the question.</li><li><strong>Them:</strong> You always do this superior thing.</li><li><strong>You:</strong> Okay.</li><li><strong>Them:</strong> So you have nothing to say?</li><li><strong>You:</strong> I’m not continuing this conversation.</li></ol>
<p>Notice the move: you do not prove that you are warm, fair, or normal. You keep the surface small until the bait has less to hold.</p>
<h2>The smallest usable version</h2>
<p>If you cannot remember a script, use the shortest line that still protects you.</p>
<div class="copy-script-box"><p>“Okay.”</p><button type="button" class="copy-line" data-copy="“Okay.”">Copy</button></div>
<p>If you need a little more shape, use:</p>
<div class="copy-script-box"><p>“I’m not discussing that.”</p><button type="button" class="copy-line" data-copy="“I’m not discussing that.”">Copy</button></div>
<p>If they keep pulling for emotion, use the exit:</p>
<div class="copy-script-box"><p>“I’m going to stop here.”</p><button type="button" class="copy-line" data-copy="“I’m going to stop here.”">Copy</button></div>
<p>Grey Rock fails when you give one short line and then donate the paragraph anyway. The smallest usable version is the line plus the stop.</p>
<h2>Sources and further reading</h2>`
    )} />

    <script>
      document.addEventListener("click", async (event) => {
        const button = event.target instanceof HTMLElement ? event.target.closest("[data-copy]") : null;
        if (!(button instanceof HTMLButtonElement)) return;
        const text = button.dataset.copy || "";
        if (!text) return;
        await navigator.clipboard?.writeText(text);
        const original = button.textContent;
        button.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = original || "Copy";
        }, 1400);
      });
    </script>
